From: Fransis <fransis@pocknix>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: poll battery capacity periodically

The Odin 3 (SM8750) battery fuel gauge runs in the ADSP firmware
(pmic_glink -> qcom_battmgr). The kernel does NOT poll: the percentage
only updates when something reads /sys/class/power_supply/battery/capacity
(which triggers a BATTMGR_BAT_PROPERTY_GET request to the firmware).

Symptoms on the Odin 3:
- The battery percentage in SteamOS/Steam UI is frozen while playing or
  navigating menus; it only refreshes when entering/exiting a game (a
  context change that forces a battery read).
- Low-battery warnings and clean shutdown never trigger on time, because
  nothing reads the battery while a game is running -> the battery drains
  to empty and the system powers off abruptly.

Fix: add a delayed_work that polls capacity + status every 30s and calls
power_supply_changed() so the power supply core emits uevents and
upower/Steam refresh the UI and low-battery logic fires.

The polling only starts once the PDR service is up (service_up), and is
cancelled when the service goes down. 30s matches other qcom battery
drivers' poll intervals.

Signed-off-by: Fransis <fransis@pocknix>
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -333,6 +333,7 @@
 	struct qcom_battmgr_wireless wireless;
 
 	struct work_struct enable_work;
+	struct delayed_work poll_work;
 
 	/*
 	 * @lock is used to prevent concurrent power supply requests to the
@@ -1599,6 +1600,23 @@
 		dev_err(battmgr->dev, "failed to request power notifications\n");
 }
 
+/*
+ * The ADSP firmware does not push periodic battery updates; the percentage
+ * only moves when something reads sysfs (which triggers a property GET to
+ * the firmware). While a game is running nothing reads the battery, so the
+ * percentage freezes and low-battery warnings never fire.
+ */
+static void qcom_battmgr_poll_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr = container_of(work, struct qcom_battmgr,
+						    poll_work.work);
+
+	qcom_battmgr_bat_sm8350_update(battmgr, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY);
+	power_supply_changed(battmgr->bat_psy);
+
+	schedule_delayed_work(&battmgr->poll_work, 30 * HZ);
+}
+
 static void qcom_battmgr_pdr_notify(void *priv, int state)
 {
 	struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr = priv;
@@ -1606,8 +1624,10 @@
 	if (state == SERVREG_SERVICE_STATE_UP) {
 		battmgr->service_up = true;
 		schedule_work(&battmgr->enable_work);
+		schedule_delayed_work(&battmgr->poll_work, 30 * HZ);
 	} else {
 		battmgr->service_up = false;
+		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&battmgr->poll_work);
 	}
 }
 
@@ -1715,6 +1735,8 @@
 				   qcom_battmgr_enable_worker);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &battmgr->poll_work,
+				     qcom_battmgr_poll_work);
 
 	battmgr->client = devm_pmic_glink_client_alloc(dev, PMIC_GLINK_OWNER_BATTMGR,
 						       qcom_battmgr_callback,
